msgid "Terminology Service (TS)"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:69
msgid "The ability to trace something. In some cases, it is interpreted as the ability to verify the history, location or application of an item by means of documented identification (14)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:38
msgid "The benefit or utility a stakeholder gains from using a service, product, or capability."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:90
msgid "The Benefits Package Registry is the national authoritative record of all health benefit packages offered within a country's health financing ecosystem. It holds the definitive description of what each package covers, who is eligible in general terms, which scheme or schemes offer it, and under what rules and conditions benefits may be accessed."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:49
msgid "The characteristics of a system that include look and feel as well as what the system can do (e.g. “reporting” can be a feature of a PCPOSS)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:80
msgid "The Client Registry is the national authoritative source of health-specific person identity. It is the foundational health-sector component that maintains a unique, verifiable identity record for every person who accesses or is eligible to access health services within a jurisdiction."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:88
msgid "The Computable Decision Support Engine is a governed, shared application component that delivers context-appropriate, evidence-based guidance at the point of clinical decision-making by applying computable clinical rules and knowledge artefacts to person-specific health data."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:79
msgid "The continuous process of collecting and analysing data to compare how well an intervention is being implemented against expected results (8)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:35
msgid "The design of a specific application component or HDPI expressed through specifications and diagrams [Under review]"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:81
msgid "The Health Facility Registry is the national authoritative source of identity, location, and classification data for all facilities, locations, and organisations through which health services are delivered or that are otherwise relevant to health system operations."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:92
msgid "The Health Management Information System is a governed, shared application component responsible for the systematic collection, aggregation, analysis, and dissemination of population-level and facility-level health data to support health system planning, performance monitoring, resource allocation, and policy decision-making."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:82
msgid "The Health Workforce Registry is the national authoritative record of identity, credential, and classification data for all health workers recognised as part of the national health workforce — including licensed or certified clinical professionals, community health workers, allied health personnel, and administrative and management staff in health-related roles."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:86
msgid "The Lifelong Health Record (LHR) is one or more governed data repositories, whether physically consolidated or virtually federated, that collectively maintain a longitudinal, person-centred record of an individual's key health information across care settings and over their lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:85
msgid "The Logical Information Model Repository is a governed, publicly accessible repository and management platform for computable clinical and administrative information models that define the logical structure, semantics, and terminology bindings of health data objects across a national digital health ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:101
msgid "The Open Group Architecture Framework (TOGAF, The Open Group Architectural Framework)"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:37
msgid "The Open Group Architecture Framework, an enterprise architecture framework and method, published by The Open Group, for developing an enterprise architecture."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:17
msgid "The organising logic for business processes and IT infrastructure reflecting the integration andstandardisation requirements of the organisation's operating model. [Under review]"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:47
msgid "The process of converting and organizing data from paper records into a digital format for easier entry, storage and retrieval (12,16)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:46
msgid "The process of digitally automating and simplifying processes to streamline individual health programmes and reduce manual efforts for greater efficiency (12,13)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:45
msgid "The process of digitally optimizing and driving systems-level changes by leveraging innovation, analytics and feedback mechanisms to improve person-centred health systems. Digital technologies are used to fundamentally change and improve how health services are delivered and accessed across all health programme areas (12,14,15)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:83
msgid "The Product Registry is the national authoritative source of core identity and classification data for health products — medicines, vaccines, medical devices, diagnostics, and health commodities — recognised for use within a jurisdiction."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:93
msgid "The Public Health Surveillance Platform is a governed, shared application component for the systematic, ongoing collection, analysis, interpretation, and dissemination of health data to detect, monitor, and respond to public health threats and events."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:68
msgid "The resources required to support a digital health intervention throughout its life cycle."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:87
msgid "The Semantic Governance Infrastructure (SGI) is the cross-cutting capability that keeps the metadata registry components accurate, consistent and trustworthy, so that the semantic consistency they are intended to provide does not degrade as the health digital ecosystem grows."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:75
msgid "The sequence of activities from one task to another (see section 3.3)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:12
msgid "The structures and standards (policies & legal frameworks) necessary to coordinate and manage the data journey from collection, storage, sharing, analysis to use to produce trusted, secure and quality data for decision making"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:89
msgid "The Supplier Registry is the authoritative master data source for identity, classification, and regulatory status of suppliers engaged in the health supply chain — including manufacturers, distributors, wholesalers, third-party logistics providers, importers, and procurement agents."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:77
msgid "The systematic and objective assessment of an ongoing or completed intervention with the aim of determining the fulfilment of objectives, efficiency, effectiveness, impact and sustainability (8)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:14
msgid "The systematic application of information and communications technologies, computer science, and data to support informed decision-making by individuals, the health workforce, and health systems, to strengthen resilience to disease and improve health and wellness."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:67
msgid "The technical framework of the system depicted in a conceptual model that defines how the system is structured and how its elements are connected."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:84
msgid "The Terminology Service is a governed, publicly accessible service that manages, publishes, and provides access to the standardised terminologies, code systems, value sets, and concept maps used across the digital health ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:37
msgid "TOGAF"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md:68
msgid "Total Cost of Ownership (TCO, total cost of ownership)"
msgstr ""

